cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes or data, please cite this software as given below."
title: "cubic-ghost-quantisation: spectrum and positive metrics of the cubic ghost oscillator"
abstract: >-
  Python codes and data accompanying the article "Spectrum and positive metrics of the cubic
  ghost oscillator" by D. Batic and D. Dutykh. They compute the spectra of finite compressions
  of the cubic ghost generator of Holdom, which is similar to the imaginary cubic oscillator,
  in double precision with condition numbers and residuals; its lowest 31 real levels from
  determinants of large compressions in decimal arithmetic of 100 to 140 digits, checked by a
  finite-difference calculation in coordinate space; and the finite-matrix check of the
  complex-pair weights and of the sum rule of the two-point function.
type: software
